## System Overview

The cantilever characterisation system is designed to measure the free-vibration response of a cantilever and determine its natural frequency, damping ratio, and quality factor.

The system consists of two main parts: the optical measurement path and the electrical signal-processing path.

### Optical Path

The optical lever uses a laser beam directed towards the vibrating cantilever. The reflected beam is guided using two mirrors and falls on a Position Sensitive Detector (PSD). When the cantilever vibrates, its small angular movement causes a corresponding displacement of the laser spot on the PSD.

